Add NVIDIA NVENC (h264_nvenc) H264 encoder for KPipeWire 6.8.3

On NVIDIA the VAAPI driver is decode-only, so H264VAAPIEncoder cannot
encode and KPipeWire falls back to CPU libx264. Add H264NvencEncoder,
which uses a zero-copy GPU pipeline when an NVIDIA EGL/CUDA render node
is available: DMA-BUF frames are imported via a bounded LRU EGLImage
cache (keyed by DMA-BUF dev/inode), converted to BT.709 NV12 (full or
limited range, padded to even dimensions) in a single-pass OpenGL 4.3
compute shader (with a 2-pass GL 3.3 fragment fallback), copied
VRAM-to-VRAM into a pooled AV_PIX_FMT_CUDA frame via CUDA-GL interop
(libcuda.so.1 loaded dynamically), and encoded directly by h264_nvenc
with zero PCIe round-trip or CPU swscale.

Falls back cleanly to a non-debug, EGLImage-cached GL_BGRA downloader
for hybrid multi-GPU DMA-BUFs (e.g. Intel/AMD compositor + NVIDIA NVENC),
or a pooled single-pass NV12 software path when GPU interop is unavailable
(or KPIPEWIRE_NVENC_NO_ZEROCOPY=1 is set).

Also configures h264_nvenc with explicit profile, spatial AQ, disabled
unused SEI side-data, zero-latency options (zerolatency=1, delay=0,
multipass=disabled, surfaces=8) for Speed/NoPreference, live runtime
setQuality() VBR/VBV reconfiguration, persistent AVPacket/AVFrame reuse,
env tuning overrides (KPIPEWIRE_NVENC_{PRESET,TUNE,CQ,MAXRATE,GOP,
SPATIAL_AQ,INTRA_REFRESH}), per-second stage-timing and bitrate telemetry
under kpipewire_record_framestatistics, sub-millisecond frame pacing,
lost wakeup fixes, and inline packet draining for video-only streams.

Tried before the VAAPI path; force with KPIPEWIRE_FORCE_ENCODER=h264_nvenc.

